  "details": "So I've seen this with finalIK scripts and other games that support lower body tracking, but I think that if your feet go out of range of where your feet can logically be IK'd, instead of just not being able to go any further, the tracker should instead represent the toes at this point and have the feet try and IK to the tracker's position using the toe instead, this behavior would of course only be noticable when stretching your leg out as far as humanly possible.",
